===Terminals===
====Passenger====
<!--EAST A]=B=D=E=F=G=[HI]=J=K=L=M=N=[O WEST-->
BYL Airport has 3 terminals and 14 concourses with a total of ### gates. The Domestic Terminal is located on the east side, the International Terminal on the west side, and the Transit Terminal in the middle of the airport. The Transit Terminal is effectively split into two sections, east and west, which are known as Transit Terminal Domestic (east) and Transit Terminal International (west). Concourse A is directly connected to the Domestic Terminal, Concourse O to the International Terminal, Concourse H to the Transit Terminal Domestic, and Concourse I to the Transit Terminal International. The remaining 10 concourses (Concourses B-G and J-N) are located between the three terminals and are parallel to one another. Together, Concourses A-H are the Domestic zone of the airport, while Concourses I-O are the International zone. The terminals and concourses are connected airside by an underground pedestrian tunnel with a series of moving walkways and by two 24/7 underground [[wikipedia:people mover|automated people movers]], one for the Domestic zone and the other for the International zone. 

[[QMR]]'s hub includes operations on all 14 concourses. Concourses A-H are mainly used by that airline for domestic flights, on which it has a state monopoly, but also by certain [[Meran]]ian airlines whose country of origin has border pre-clearance facilities for Qym. As such, passengers on flights from those countries have already gone through Qymish customs when they arrive in Zhol, resulting in those flights being treated as domestic flights. 

====Cargo====
The Cargo Terminal is located to the north of the airport, between runways 9L/27R and 9R/27L. 

===On-Site Hotels===
BYL Airport has three hotels within its terminals: a [[QYMISH HOTEL BRAND]] in the Domestic Terminal, a [[LUXURY HOTEL BRAND]] in the Transit Terminal, and a [[INTERNATIONAL HOTEL BRAND]] in the International Terminal. 

